<title>USA: Apple cuts some prices up to 27 percent.</title>
<headline>Apple cuts some prices up to 27 percent.</headline>
<dateline>CUPERTINO, Calif. 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Apple Computer Inc said it cut prices of products in most of its personal computer lines by up to 27 percent, as part of a pledge to keep its machines competitive in price.</p>
<p>The third-biggest U.S. maker of personal computers cut prices on some models of its high-end Power Macintosh, its consumer-oriented Performa and its business-oriented Workgroup Servers.</p>
<p>The price of the high-end Power Macintosh 9500/200, for example, was reduced to about $3,200 from $4,200.</p>
